@* Hexagon "VI" crest — the brand mark used in the nav, footer and elsewhere (brief §8: simple,
   symmetric, legible small). Redrawn to match the studio mark: a double hexagon border, "THE VI"
   above the monogram, and the gold pin-and-diamond flourish either side of it.

   Everything but the gold accent rides on currentColor rather than a fixed green, which is what
   lets the one mark drop onto a dark header, a faded hero watermark (color: var(--vih-line-on-dark))
   or a muted cream empty-state icon (color: var(--vih-green-900)) without a second colour to manage
   per context — see _nav.scss, _footer.scss, _admin.scss and _home.scss for each of those. The gold
   is the one brand accent used the same way regardless of ground (chips, borders, badges elsewhere
   on the site), so it is the one place this mark is never currentColor. *@
<svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" role="img" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
    <polygon points="50,4 91,27 91,73 50,96 9,73 9,27" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3" />
    <polygon points="50,13 83,32 83,68 50,87 17,68 17,32" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" />

    <text x="50" y="26" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Georgia, 'Playfair Display', serif" font-style="italic" font-size="8" letter-spacing="3" fill="currentColor">THE VI</text>
    <text x="50" y="66" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Georgia, 'Playfair Display', serif" font-size="34" font-weight="700" fill="currentColor">VI</text>

    <g stroke="var(--vih-gold)" fill="none" stroke-width="1.2">
        <circle cx="22" cy="53" r="2" />
        <line x1="24" y1="53" x2="30" y2="53" />
        <circle cx="78" cy="53" r="2" />
        <line x1="76" y1="53" x2="70" y2="53" />
    </g>
    <g fill="var(--vih-gold)">
        <rect x="28" y="51" width="4" height="4" transform="rotate(45 30 53)" />
        <rect x="66" y="51" width="4" height="4" transform="rotate(45 68 53)" />
        <rect x="48" y="76" width="4" height="4" transform="rotate(45 50 78)" />
    </g>
</svg>
